From: harlan <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Enable FMC chip-select 1 for backup BMC flash on TiogaPass

The AST2500 FMC controller supports two chip selects. CS0 holds the primary
BMC flash (the "bmc" partition); CS1 is the second SPI socket used as a cold-
boot backup device. Enable flash@1 with label "bmc-backup" so /sbin/backup-bmc-flash
can find and write the chip via flashcp.

The chip is not pre-partitioned (the full image is written from offset 0), so
no sub-partitions are declared. The MTD layer exposes the whole chip as a
single device labelled "bmc-backup".
---
 .../boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/aspeed/aspeed-bmc-facebook-tiogapass.dts
@@ -105,6 +105,17 @@
 		m25p,fast-read;
 #include "openbmc-flash-layout-64-tioga.dtsi"
 	};
+
+	flash@1 {
+		status = "okay";
+		label = "bmc-backup";
+		m25p,fast-read;
+		spi-max-frequency = <50000000>;
+		/*
+		 * No sub-partitions: backup-bmc-flash writes the full
+		 * static.mtd image from offset 0 of the chip.
+		 */
+	};
 };

 &spi1 {
